    "details": "NLNetLabs reports:\n\n> This release consolidates security fixes for issues reported over a\n> period of time.\n>\n> - CVE-2026-97206, DoQ path-migration can lead to use-after-free on\n>   multi-threaded deployments.\n> - CVE-2026-50106, Possible insecure NXDOMAIN for non-existing records\n>   under a configured island trust anchor underneath an insecure\n>   parent.\n> - CVE-2026-96405, Aggregate DNS name chained pointer decompression\n>   work leads to degradation of service.\n> - CVE-2026-109125, Possible cache poisoning vulnerability via a cache\n>   side-channel exposed by 'unwanted-reply-threshold'.\n> - CVE-2026-35501, Bypass of a configured island trust anchor\n>   underneath an insecure parent from an attacker-controlled NSEC\n>   record.\n",
